(1423691, 182751, 14986, '<td valign="top">Beauty is a subjective thing, I know.  In my scoring and comments I''m trying to score based on NOT whether or not I would think a particular subject beautiful, but on whether the photographer has succeeded in creating a beautiful photo.  I look for the elements of color, lines, focus and dof interest, lighting,  and a certain element of grace and lovlieness.   I''m looking for a unique and creative  appeal for the highest scorers.   (This is what I''m putting at the start of all of my comments,  and I hope it is helpful.)<br/> <br/>That being said,  probably my first thought was that I wished this had more of a portrait orientation to sort of follow the movement of the water.  It feel crowded at the top of the frame over the water.  I really like the subject, the lighting, exposure and good focus and stop action.  The tones, eh.  I''m not sure on that one.   Fits the challenge well.<br/></td>', 'Beauty is a subjective thing, I know.  In my scoring and comments I''m trying to score based on NOT whether or not I would think a particular subject beautiful, but on whether the photographer has succeeded in creating a beautiful photo.  I look for the elements of color, lines, focus and dof interest, lighting,  and a certain element of grace and lovlieness.   I''m looking for a unique and creative  appeal for the highest scorers.   (This is what I''m putting at the start of all of my comments,  and I hope it is helpful.) That being said,  probably my first thought was that I wished this had more of a portrait orientation to sort of follow the movement of the water.  It feel crowded at the top of the frame over the water.  I really like the subject, the lighting, exposure and good focus and stop action.  The tones, eh.  I''m not sure on that one.   Fits the challenge well.', '2005-05-31 17:20:13.000000', NULL, 1),
