(1424685, 181311, 14986, '<td valign="top">Beauty is a subjective thing, I know.  In my scoring and comments I''m trying to score based on NOT whether or not I would think a particular subject beautiful, but on whether the photographer has succeeded in creating a beautiful photo.  I look for the elements of color, lines, focus and dof interest, lighting,  and a certain element of grace and lovlieness.   I''m looking for a unique and creative  appeal for the highest scorers.  The description says to create a photo that makes the viewer think "that''s beautiful", so it will undoubtedly be very subjective.   (This is what I''m putting at the start of all of my comments,  and I hope it is helpful.)<br/> <br/>That being said,I do like the soft focus here.  I think it helps to add some feeling to a typical flower shot.  It''s pretty and it fits the challenge, but I don''t find it particularly creative or unique.</td>', 'Beauty is a subjective thing, I know.  In my scoring and comments I''m trying to score based on NOT whether or not I would think a particular subject beautiful, but on whether the photographer has succeeded in creating a beautiful photo.  I look for the elements of color, lines, focus and dof interest, lighting,  and a certain element of grace and lovlieness.   I''m looking for a unique and creative  appeal for the highest scorers.  The description says to create a photo that makes the viewer think "that''s beautiful", so it will undoubtedly be very subjective.   (This is what I''m putting at the start of all of my comments,  and I hope it is helpful.) That being said,I do like the soft focus here.  I think it helps to add some feeling to a typical flower shot.  It''s pretty and it fits the challenge, but I don''t find it particularly creative or unique.', '2005-06-01 00:52:31.000000', NULL, 1),
(1424691, 182763, 25433, '<td valign="top">This image kicks significant arse. Beautifully composed and colours manificient. The slightly soft wing doesn''t bother me, seems to add to the depth. Well done.</td>', 'This image kicks significant arse. Beautifully composed and colours manificient. The slightly soft wing doesn''t bother me, seems to add to the depth. Well done.', '2005-06-01 00:54:15.000000', NULL, 1),
(1424692, 183181, 14986, '<td valign="top">Beauty is a subjective thing, I know.  In my scoring and comments I''m trying to score based on NOT whether or not I would think a particular subject beautiful, but on whether the photographer has succeeded in creating a beautiful photo.  I look for the elements of color, lines, focus and dof interest, lighting,  and a certain element of grace and lovlieness.   I''m looking for a unique and creative  appeal for the highest scorers.  The description says to create a photo that makes the viewer think "that''s beautiful", so it will undoubtedly be very subjective.   (This is what I''m putting at the start of all of my comments,  and I hope it is helpful.)<br/> <br/>That being said,  this has a few really nice elements:  the sky of course, the sillohuettes of the trees, the reflections and the water and the ducks in the foreground.  I don''t see this as a particularly unique or creative photo, but the view is certainly well above average!</td>', 'Beauty is a subjective thing, I know.  In my scoring and comments I''m trying to score based on NOT whether or not I would think a particular subject beautiful, but on whether the photographer has succeeded in creating a beautiful photo.  I look for the elements of color, lines, focus and dof interest, lighting,  and a certain element of grace and lovlieness.   I''m looking for a unique and creative  appeal for the highest scorers.  The description says to create a photo that makes the viewer think "that''s beautiful", so it will undoubtedly be very subjective.   (This is what I''m putting at the start of all of my comments,  and I hope it is helpful.) That being said,  this has a few really nice elements:  the sky of course, the sillohuettes of the trees, the reflections and the water and the ducks in the foreground.  I don''t see this as a particularly unique or creative photo, but the view is certainly well above average!', '2005-06-01 00:54:35.000000', NULL, 1),
(1424698, 183176, 25433, '<td valign="top">Thats a big bugger. Despite the title, doesn''t scream "Beautiful". Lovely macro though, scares the crap out of me. [8]</td>', 'Thats a big bugger. Despite the title, doesn''t scream "Beautiful". Lovely macro though, scares the crap out of me. [8]', '2005-06-01 00:56:40.000000', NULL, 1),
(1424700, 183149, 14986, '<td valign="top">Beauty is a subjective thing, I know.  In my scoring and comments I''m trying to score based on NOT whether or not I would think a particular subject beautiful, but on whether the photographer has succeeded in creating a beautiful photo.  I look for the elements of color, lines, focus and dof interest, lighting,  and a certain element of grace and lovlieness.   I''m looking for a unique and creative  appeal for the highest scorers.  The description says to create a photo that makes the viewer think "that''s beautiful", so it will undoubtedly be very subjective.   (This is what I''m putting at the start of all of my comments,  and I hope it is helpful.)<br/> <br/>That being said,  This is a very nice shot.  I think I would have titled it "freckles" and they are lovely!  I really like the turn of the head, the expression and the movement of the head.  I''d like to see improvements in the lighting on the face. I like that you have some shadow and light, but I wish we had some light on the eyes.  Overall, a real beauty.</td>', 'Beauty is a subjective thing, I know.  In my scoring and comments I''m trying to score based on NOT whether or not I would think a particular subject beautiful, but on whether the photographer has succeeded in creating a beautiful photo.  I look for the elements of color, lines, focus and dof interest, lighting,  and a certain element of grace and lovlieness.   I''m looking for a unique and creative  appeal for the highest scorers.  The description says to create a photo that makes the viewer think "that''s beautiful", so it will undoubtedly be very subjective.   (This is what I''m putting at the start of all of my comments,  and I hope it is helpful.) That being said,  This is a very nice shot.  I think I would have titled it "freckles" and they are lovely!  I really like the turn of the head, the expression and the movement of the head.  I''d like to see improvements in the lighting on the face. I like that you have some shadow and light, but I wish we had some light on the eyes.  Overall, a real beauty.', '2005-06-01 00:57:02.000000', NULL, 1),
(1424704, 182782, 38007, '<td valign="top">Beautiful...a 10 without the frame.</td>', 'Beautiful...a 10 without the frame.', '2005-06-01 00:58:27.000000', NULL, 1),
(1424706, 182662, 14986, '<td valign="top">Beauty is a subjective thing, I know.  In my scoring and comments I''m trying to score based on NOT whether or not I would think a particular subject beautiful, but on whether the photographer has succeeded in creating a beautiful photo.  I look for the elements of color, lines, focus and dof interest, lighting,  and a certain element of grace and lovlieness.   I''m looking for a unique and creative  appeal for the highest scorers.  The description says to create a photo that makes the viewer think "that''s beautiful", so it will undoubtedly be very subjective.   (This is what I''m putting at the start of all of my comments,  and I hope it is helpful.)<br/> <br/>That being said,  this is a slightly different approach to a floral shot and I think it works well with this particular bloom.   I like the bit of faded color from the bloom in the background as well.  For composition, I would like a little bit more cropped off the top, but that''s really a matter of taste.  Nice color and decent focus although not super clear.  Above average for the floral shots IMO.</td>', 'Beauty is a subjective thing, I know.  In my scoring and comments I''m trying to score based on NOT whether or not I would think a particular subject beautiful, but on whether the photographer has succeeded in creating a beautiful photo.  I look for the elements of color, lines, focus and dof interest, lighting,  and a certain element of grace and lovlieness.   I''m looking for a unique and creative  appeal for the highest scorers.  The description says to create a photo that makes the viewer think "that''s beautiful", so it will undoubtedly be very subjective.   (This is what I''m putting at the start of all of my comments,  and I hope it is helpful.) That being said,  this is a slightly different approach to a floral shot and I think it works well with this particular bloom.   I like the bit of faded color from the bloom in the background as well.  For composition, I would like a little bit more cropped off the top, but that''s really a matter of taste.  Nice color and decent focus although not super clear.  Above average for the floral shots IMO.', '2005-06-01 00:59:24.000000', NULL, 1),
(1424712, 182153, 14986, '<td valign="top">Beauty is a subjective thing, I know.  In my scoring and comments I''m trying to score based on NOT whether or not I would think a particular subject beautiful, but on whether the photographer has succeeded in creating a beautiful photo.  I look for the elements of color, lines, focus and dof interest, lighting,  and a certain element of grace and lovlieness.   I''m looking for a unique and creative  appeal for the highest scorers.  The description says to create a photo that makes the viewer think "that''s beautiful", so it will undoubtedly be very subjective.   (This is what I''m putting at the start of all of my comments,  and I hope it is helpful.)<br/> <br/>That being said,  this is a wonderful capture of the eagle in flight.  Nice dof, very nice light and colors.  Certainly a majestic and beautiful subject.   I keep wondering what was around it, as the vertical crop seems a bit severe, but there may have been a reason for that.   One of my favorites so far.</td>', 'Beauty is a subjective thing, I know.  In my scoring and comments I''m trying to score based on NOT whether or not I would think a particular subject beautiful, but on whether the photographer has succeeded in creating a beautiful photo.  I look for the elements of color, lines, focus and dof interest, lighting,  and a certain element of grace and lovlieness.   I''m looking for a unique and creative  appeal for the highest scorers.  The description says to create a photo that makes the viewer think "that''s beautiful", so it will undoubtedly be very subjective.   (This is what I''m putting at the start of all of my comments,  and I hope it is helpful.) That being said,  this is a wonderful capture of the eagle in flight.  Nice dof, very nice light and colors.  Certainly a majestic and beautiful subject.   I keep wondering what was around it, as the vertical crop seems a bit severe, but there may have been a reason for that.   One of my favorites so far.', '2005-06-01 01:01:20.000000', NULL, 1),
(1424723, 182998, 38007, '<td valign="top">puppy is distractingly out of focus.</td>', 'puppy is distractingly out of focus.', '2005-06-01 01:03:38.000000', NULL, 1),
(1424732, 183052, 14986, '<td valign="top">Beauty is a subjective thing, I know.  In my scoring and comments I''m trying to score based on NOT whether or not I would think a particular subject beautiful, but on whether the photographer has succeeded in creating a beautiful photo.  I look for the elements of color, lines, focus and dof interest, lighting,  and a certain element of grace and lovlieness.   I''m looking for a unique and creative  appeal for the highest scorers.  The description says to create a photo that makes the viewer think "that''s beautiful", so it will undoubtedly be very subjective.   (This is what I''m putting at the start of all of my comments,  and I hope it is helpful.)<br/> <br/>That being said, this is a lovely subject, but I don''t see it as being photographed in a particularly unique or creative way.  Colors are nice, but the composition seems to suffer some, imo.  I would crop the right side to totally get rid of the dark background and a lot of the blown out white on that side, and focus on the wonderful colors of the interior portion of the bloom.  Focus also seems a little soft, which may have been intentional, but if it was I don''t think it adds to the photo.  Really pretty flower to photograph.</td>', 'Beauty is a subjective thing, I know.  In my scoring and comments I''m trying to score based on NOT whether or not I would think a particular subject beautiful, but on whether the photographer has succeeded in creating a beautiful photo.  I look for the elements of color, lines, focus and dof interest, lighting,  and a certain element of grace and lovlieness.   I''m looking for a unique and creative  appeal for the highest scorers.  The description says to create a photo that makes the viewer think "that''s beautiful", so it will undoubtedly be very subjective.   (This is what I''m putting at the start of all of my comments,  and I hope it is helpful.) That being said, this is a lovely subject, but I don''t see it as being photographed in a particularly unique or creative way.  Colors are nice, but the composition seems to suffer some, imo.  I would crop the right side to totally get rid of the dark background and a lot of the blown out white on that side, and focus on the wonderful colors of the interior portion of the bloom.  Focus also seems a little soft, which may have been intentional, but if it was I don''t think it adds to the photo.  Really pretty flower to photograph.', '2005-06-01 01:04:32.000000', NULL, 1),
(1424746, 183331, 38007, '<td valign="top">OK this could be the best!</td>', 'OK this could be the best!', '2005-06-01 01:06:15.000000', NULL, 1),
(1424750, 183137, 14986, '<td valign="top">Beauty is a subjective thing, I know.  In my scoring and comments I''m trying to score based on NOT whether or not I would think a particular subject beautiful, but on whether the photographer has succeeded in creating a beautiful photo.  I look for the elements of color, lines, focus and dof interest, lighting,  and a certain element of grace and lovlieness.   I''m looking for a unique and creative  appeal for the highest scorers.  The description says to create a photo that makes the viewer think "that''s beautiful", so it will undoubtedly be very subjective.   (This is what I''m putting at the start of all of my comments,  and I hope it is helpful.)<br/> <br/>That being said,  this is a cute subject and beautiful in nature.  I do think the photo suffers some on the technical aspects.  The face seems out of focus with some rather odd glaring sort of lighting.  There also seems to be a purplish tinit that distracts from the doe.</td>', 'Beauty is a subjective thing, I know.  In my scoring and comments I''m trying to score based on NOT whether or not I would think a particular subject beautiful, but on whether the photographer has succeeded in creating a beautiful photo.  I look for the elements of color, lines, focus and dof interest, lighting,  and a certain element of grace and lovlieness.   I''m looking for a unique and creative  appeal for the highest scorers.  The description says to create a photo that makes the viewer think "that''s beautiful", so it will undoubtedly be very subjective.   (This is what I''m putting at the start of all of my comments,  and I hope it is helpful.) That being said,  this is a cute subject and beautiful in nature.  I do think the photo suffers some on the technical aspects.  The face seems out of focus with some rather odd glaring sort of lighting.  There also seems to be a purplish tinit that distracts from the doe.', '2005-06-01 01:06:48.000000', NULL, 1),
(1424760, 183340, 14986, '<td valign="top">Beauty is a subjective thing, I know.  In my scoring and comments I''m trying to score based on NOT whether or not I would think a particular subject beautiful, but on whether the photographer has succeeded in creating a beautiful photo.  I look for the elements of color, lines, focus and dof interest, lighting,  and a certain element of grace and lovlieness.   I''m looking for a unique and creative  appeal for the highest scorers.  The description says to create a photo that makes the viewer think "that''s beautiful", so it will undoubtedly be very subjective.   (This is what I''m putting at the start of all of my comments,  and I hope it is helpful.)<br/> <br/>That being said,  I think I might find this more appealing in person.  The tones here seem really hot and arid.  The large grouping of trees on the right rather dominate the photo and don''t add a lot to the appeal.  I would have liked something with more view of the water.   For me, though, those orangish tones are the biggest drawback to thinking "beauty".</td>', 'Beauty is a subjective thing, I know.  In my scoring and comments I''m trying to score based on NOT whether or not I would think a particular subject beautiful, but on whether the photographer has succeeded in creating a beautiful photo.  I look for the elements of color, lines, focus and dof interest, lighting,  and a certain element of grace and lovlieness.   I''m looking for a unique and creative  appeal for the highest scorers.  The description says to create a photo that makes the viewer think "that''s beautiful", so it will undoubtedly be very subjective.   (This is what I''m putting at the start of all of my comments,  and I hope it is helpful.) That being said,  I think I might find this more appealing in person.  The tones here seem really hot and arid.  The large grouping of trees on the right rather dominate the photo and don''t add a lot to the appeal.  I would have liked something with more view of the water.   For me, though, those orangish tones are the biggest drawback to thinking "beauty".', '2005-06-01 01:08:57.000000', NULL, 1),
(1424772, 181386, 14986, '<td valign="top">Beauty is a subjective thing, I know.  In my scoring and comments I''m trying to score based on NOT whether or not I would think a particular subject beautiful, but on whether the photographer has succeeded in creating a beautiful photo.  I look for the elements of color, lines, focus and dof interest, lighting,  and a certain element of grace and lovlieness.   I''m looking for a unique and creative  appeal for the highest scorers.  The description says to create a photo that makes the viewer think "that''s beautiful", so it will undoubtedly be very subjective.   (This is what I''m putting at the start of all of my comments,  and I hope it is helpful.)<br/> <br/>That being said, this looks like a lovely location.  It also is probably more appealing in person than the photo actually shows.  It just doesn''t seem to capture anything particularly interesting imo.  Maybe if you picked up a bit more detail in the dark foreground, it would help.</td>', 'Beauty is a subjective thing, I know.  In my scoring and comments I''m trying to score based on NOT whether or not I would think a particular subject beautiful, but on whether the photographer has succeeded in creating a beautiful photo.  I look for the elements of color, lines, focus and dof interest, lighting,  and a certain element of grace and lovlieness.   I''m looking for a unique and creative  appeal for the highest scorers.  The description says to create a photo that makes the viewer think "that''s beautiful", so it will undoubtedly be very subjective.   (This is what I''m putting at the start of all of my comments,  and I hope it is helpful.) That being said, this looks like a lovely location.  It also is probably more appealing in person than the photo actually shows.  It just doesn''t seem to capture anything particularly interesting imo.  Maybe if you picked up a bit more detail in the dark foreground, it would help.', '2005-06-01 01:10:27.000000', NULL, 1),
