', NULL, 1),
(1424799, 182844, 14986, '<td valign="top">Beauty is a subjective thing, I know.  In my scoring and comments I''m trying to score based on NOT whether or not I would think a particular subject beautiful, but on whether the photographer has succeeded in creating a beautiful photo.  I look for the elements of color, lines, focus and dof interest, lighting,  and a certain element of grace and lovlieness.   I''m looking for a unique and creative  appeal for the highest scorers.  The description says to create a photo that makes the viewer think "that''s beautiful", so it will undoubtedly be very subjective.   (This is what I''m putting at the start of all of my comments,  and I hope it is helpful.)<br/> <br/>That being said,  this is one of my favorites so far.  I''m not a fan of selective desat, but I like it here a lot.  The whole concept of media and portrayal of beauty is captured in a very creative and unique way.  Perfect  placement of her "peeking" between the buildings.  Good job!</td>', 'Beauty is a subjective thing, I know.  In my scoring and comments I''m trying to score based on NOT whether or not I would think a particular subject beautiful, but on whether the photographer has succeeded in creating a beautiful photo.  I look for the elements of color, lines, focus and dof interest, lighting,  and a certain element of grace and lovlieness.   I''m looking for a unique and creative  appeal for the highest scorers.  The description says to create a photo that makes the viewer think "that''s beautiful", so it will undoubtedly be very subjective.   (This is what I''m putting at the start of all of my comments,  and I hope it is helpful.) That being said,  this is one of my favorites so far.  I''m not a fan of selective desat, but I like it here a lot.  The whole concept of media and portrayal of beauty is captured in a very creative and unique way.  Perfect  placement of her "peeking" between the buildings.  Good job!', '2005-06-01 01:14:01.000000', NULL, 1),
