(1424834, 182111, 14986, '<td valign="top">Beauty is a subjective thing, I know.  In my scoring and comments I''m trying to score based on NOT whether or not I would think a particular subject beautiful, but on whether the photographer has succeeded in creating a beautiful photo.  I look for the elements of color, lines, focus and dof interest, lighting,  and a certain element of grace and lovlieness.   I''m looking for a unique and creative  appeal for the highest scorers.  The description says to create a photo that makes the viewer think "that''s beautiful", so it will undoubtedly be very subjective.   (This is what I''m putting at the start of all of my comments,  and I hope it is helpful.)<br/> <br/>That being said,  nice subject here.   She sure has some whiskers!  :)   I really like the time of day and the lighting and I like the movement of the mane.   Just doesn''t seem to have any "wow" factor that makes me think "beauty".</td>', 'Beauty is a subjective thing, I know.  In my scoring and comments I''m trying to score based on NOT whether or not I would think a particular subject beautiful, but on whether the photographer has succeeded in creating a beautiful photo.  I look for the elements of color, lines, focus and dof interest, lighting,  and a certain element of grace and lovlieness.   I''m looking for a unique and creative  appeal for the highest scorers.  The description says to create a photo that makes the viewer think "that''s beautiful", so it will undoubtedly be very subjective.   (This is what I''m putting at the start of all of my comments,  and I hope it is helpful.) That being said,  nice subject here.   She sure has some whiskers!  :)   I really like the time of day and the lighting and I like the movement of the mane.   Just doesn''t seem to have any "wow" factor that makes me think "beauty".', '2005-06-01 01:18:58.000000', NULL, 1),
(1424839, 183165, 31742, '<td valign="top">Love the colors</td>', 'Love the colors', '2005-06-01 01:19:40.000000', NULL, 1),
(1424859, 182720, 14986, '<td valign="top">Beauty is a subjective thing, I know.  In my scoring and comments I''m trying to score based on NOT whether or not I would think a particular subject beautiful, but on whether the photographer has succeeded in creating a beautiful photo.  I look for the elements of color, lines, focus and dof interest, lighting,  and a certain element of grace and lovlieness.   I''m looking for a unique and creative  appeal for the highest scorers.  The description says to create a photo that makes the viewer think "that''s beautiful", so it will undoubtedly be very subjective.   (This is what I''m putting at the start of all of my comments,  and I hope it is helpful.)<br/> <br/>That being said,  I think this photo could be improved in several ways.  First I would either capture more of whatever that right hand branch is attached to, or get it out of the photo altogether with either a different angle or clone it out.  I think there is too much dark foreground adding nothing to the interest of the shot.  I would cut it by about half.   I know you''re shooting into the sun, but I would like to see a bit darker exposure and use your editing to bring a bit more richness to the other sky colors while reducing the sun brightness some.  And also, having both the horizon and the sun centered so much doesn''t add any composition interest at all.   I hope this is helpful.</td>', 'Beauty is a subjective thing, I know.  In my scoring and comments I''m trying to score based on NOT whether or not I would think a particular subject beautiful, but on whether the photographer has succeeded in creating a beautiful photo.  I look for the elements of color, lines, focus and dof interest, lighting,  and a certain element of grace and lovlieness.   I''m looking for a unique and creative  appeal for the highest scorers.  The description says to create a photo that makes the viewer think "that''s beautiful", so it will undoubtedly be very subjective.   (This is what I''m putting at the start of all of my comments,  and I hope it is helpful.) That being said,  I think this photo could be improved in several ways.  First I would either capture more of whatever that right hand branch is attached to, or get it out of the photo altogether with either a different angle or clone it out.  I think there is too much dark foreground adding nothing to the interest of the shot.  I would cut it by about half.   I know you''re shooting into the sun, but I would like to see a bit darker exposure and use your editing to bring a bit more richness to the other sky colors while reducing the sun brightness some.  And also, having both the horizon and the sun centered so much doesn''t add any composition interest at all.   I hope this is helpful.', '2005-06-01 01:22:24.000000', NULL, 1),
(1424886, 182546, 14986, '<td valign="top">Beauty is a subjective thing, I know.  In my scoring and comments I''m trying to score based on NOT whether or not I would think a particular subject beautiful, but on whether the photographer has succeeded in creating a beautiful photo.  I look for the elements of color, lines, focus and dof interest, lighting,  and a certain element of grace and lovlieness.   I''m looking for a unique and creative  appeal for the highest scorers.  The description says to create a photo that makes the viewer think "that''s beautiful", so it will undoubtedly be very subjective.   (This is what I''m putting at the start of all of my comments,  and I hope it is helpful.)<br/> <br/>That being said,  this is an interesting choice of subject.  The shot itself, while technically okay, seems pretty straighforward and unimaginative.  It does not seem to work to bring out the real beauty of this wood.  It seems like you saw the wood, stopped, took a shot and went on.  As a viewer, I don''t feel like a lot of effort went into trying to find a way to convey the real beauty in the subject.  I may be totally wrong, so please don''t be offended.  I''m trying to explain my reaction to the photo.</td>', 'Beauty is a subjective thing, I know.  In my scoring and comments I''m trying to score based on NOT whether or not I would think a particular subject beautiful, but on whether the photographer has succeeded in creating a beautiful photo.  I look for the elements of color, lines, focus and dof interest, lighting,  and a certain element of grace and lovlieness.   I''m looking for a unique and creative  appeal for the highest scorers.  The description says to create a photo that makes the viewer think "that''s beautiful", so it will undoubtedly be very subjective.   (This is what I''m putting at the start of all of my comments,  and I hope it is helpful.) That being said,  this is an interesting choice of subject.  The shot itself, while technically okay, seems pretty straighforward and unimaginative.  It does not seem to work to bring out the real beauty of this wood.  It seems like you saw the wood, stopped, took a shot and went on.  As a viewer, I don''t feel like a lot of effort went into trying to find a way to convey the real beauty in the subject.  I may be totally wrong, so please don''t be offended.  I''m trying to explain my reaction to the photo.', '2005-06-01 01:26:28.000000', NULL, 1),
(1424896, 183242, 14986, '<td valign="top">Beauty is a subjective thing, I know.  In my scoring and comments I''m trying to score based on NOT whether or not I would think a particular subject beautiful, but on whether the photographer has succeeded in creating a beautiful photo.  I look for the elements of color, lines, focus and dof interest, lighting,  and a certain element of grace and lovlieness.   I''m looking for a unique and creative  appeal for the highest scorers.  The description says to create a photo that makes the viewer think "that''s beautiful", so it will undoubtedly be very subjective.   (This is what I''m putting at the start of all of my comments,  and I hope it is helpful.)<br/> <br/>That being said,  you have a cute subject here!  Definitely on the prowl!  The photo itself seems out of focus and more like a hurried click than a real attempt to create and convey beauty.</td>', 'Beauty is a subjective thing, I know.  In my scoring and comments I''m trying to score based on NOT whether or not I would think a particular subject beautiful, but on whether the photographer has succeeded in creating a beautiful photo.  I look for the elements of color, lines, focus and dof interest, lighting,  and a certain element of grace and lovlieness.   I''m looking for a unique and creative  appeal for the highest scorers.  The description says to create a photo that makes the viewer think "that''s beautiful", so it will undoubtedly be very subjective.   (This is what I''m putting at the start of all of my comments,  and I hope it is helpful.) That being said,  you have a cute subject here!  Definitely on the prowl!  The photo itself seems out of focus and more like a hurried click than a real attempt to create and convey beauty.', '2005-06-01 01:28:04.000000', NULL, 1),
(1424905, 183335, 14986, '<td valign="top">Beauty is a subjective thing, I know.  In my scoring and comments I''m trying to score based on NOT whether or not I would think a particular subject beautiful, but on whether the photographer has succeeded in creating a beautiful photo.  I look for the elements of color, lines, focus and dof interest, lighting,  and a certain element of grace and lovlieness.   I''m looking for a unique and creative  appeal for the highest scorers.  The description says to create a photo that makes the viewer think "that''s beautiful", so it will undoubtedly be very subjective.   (This is what I''m putting at the start of all of my comments,  and I hope it is helpful.)<br/> <br/>That being said,  this has a lot going for it.    Wonderful composition IMO, with the hills, reflections,  bird on the beach and lots of sky.  The colors really make this scene.  Not perhaps the most creative or unique photo for beauty, but I think it''s very well done.</td>', 'Beauty is a subjective thing, I know.  In my scoring and comments I''m trying to score based on NOT whether or not I would think a particular subject beautiful, but on whether the photographer has succeeded in creating a beautiful photo.  I look for the elements of color, lines, focus and dof interest, lighting,  and a certain element of grace and lovlieness.   I''m looking for a unique and creative  appeal for the highest scorers.  The description says to create a photo that makes the viewer think "that''s beautiful", so it will undoubtedly be very subjective.   (This is what I''m putting at the start of all of my comments,  and I hope it is helpful.) That being said,  this has a lot going for it.    Wonderful composition IMO, with the hills, reflections,  bird on the beach and lots of sky.  The colors really make this scene.  Not perhaps the most creative or unique photo for beauty, but I think it''s very well done.', '2005-06-01 01:29:48.000000', NULL, 1),
(1424921, 182763, 24921, '<td valign="top">Great photo. Love the colors on this one.</td>', 'Great photo. Love the colors on this one.', '2005-06-01 01:34:24.000000', NULL, 1),
(1425075, 183322, 15305, '<td valign="top">Beauty at its best!!!!</td>', 'Beauty at its best!!!!', '2005-06-01 02:38:28.000000', NULL, 1),
(1425231, 182153, 6999, '<td valign="top">Whilst there is no doubting the beauty of your subject, I find the photograph itself to be lacking that extra element that would really make me think ''beautiful!''. I''m not wholly sure what that might be - though certainly something more than the quite straightforward portrait presented here - perhaps more sense of the dynamic, such as a bit of motion blur in the background: this shot presents a very still feeling, presumably because a high shutter speed has wiped all sense of movement. Obviously it''s technically OK - in focus, good detail, etc, although I would say it is overall a touch too bright for impact - pulling the exposure, or brightness back a touch would add some depth and life to the tree and sky colours, and make the detailing around the head and tail more easily noticeable - but the simply technically OK isn''t enough to spark that moment of amazement when the world seems to stop for a fraction of a second. 6</td>', 'Whilst there is no doubting the beauty of your subject, I find the photograph itself to be lacking that extra element that would really make me think ''beautiful!''. I''m not wholly sure what that might be - though certainly something more than the quite straightforward portrait presented here - perhaps more sense of the dynamic, such as a bit of motion blur in the background: this shot presents a very still feeling, presumably because a high shutter speed has wiped all sense of movement. Obviously it''s technically OK - in focus, good detail, etc, although I would say it is overall a touch too bright for impact - pulling the exposure, or brightness back a touch would add some depth and life to the tree and sky colours, and make the detailing around the head and tail more easily noticeable - but the simply technically OK isn''t enough to spark that moment of amazement when the world seems to stop for a fraction of a second. 6', '2005-06-01 04:00:55.000000', NULL, 1),
(1425235, 183221, 6999, '<td valign="top">A pretty scene, certainly, if over-exposed for my taste - the colour tones could certainly be stronger for a litle less brightness and, perhaps, more contrast. DOF effective, but the shot as a whole lacks a spark of inspsiration, for me.</td>', 'A pretty scene, certainly, if over-exposed for my taste - the colour tones could certainly be stronger for a litle less brightness and, perhaps, more contrast. DOF effective, but the shot as a whole lacks a spark of inspsiration, for me.', '2005-06-01 04:05:32.000000', NULL, 1),
(1425244, 183032, 6999, '<td valign="top">Nice shooting. I wonder if you placement of that head within frame is ideal - I''d perhaps have tried to frame the whole head more cemtrally, which would move the eye, the natural point of first focus,  to a stronger place in frame, and, I think, have made a more interesting graphic contribution to the entirety of the composition of the dark line of the neck. Obviously, there may beother reasons forcing this crop, but I am talking about an ideal.<br/> <br/>None of which is to subtract from the great sense of detail and texture you''ve captured here, of course.</td>', 'Nice shooting. I wonder if you placement of that head within frame is ideal - I''d perhaps have tried to frame the whole head more cemtrally, which would move the eye, the natural point of first focus,  to a stronger place in frame, and, I think, have made a more interesting graphic contribution to the entirety of the composition of the dark line of the neck. Obviously, there may beother reasons forcing this crop, but I am talking about an ideal. None of which is to subtract from the great sense of detail and texture you''ve captured here, of course.', '2005-06-01 04:14:18.000000', NULL, 1),
(1425246, 183335, 36956, '<td valign="top">lol a stunning shot... you are really good at using the purple and pink colors my man... haha... pretty much we both won a million dollars in scholarships this evening... haha, good work... nice shot too...</td>', 'lol a stunning shot... you are really good at using the purple and pink colors my man... haha... pretty much we both won a million dollars in scholarships this evening... haha, good work... nice shot too...', '2005-06-01 04:16:35.000000', NULL, 1),
(1425247, 183342, 6999, '<td valign="top">I often wonder, in shots that contain this optical illusion, whether it isn''t worth slightly over-rotating the whole thing to counter-act that. A touch darker overall would deepen the colour-tones here, which would be of use to the shot as a whole I think.</td>', 'I often wonder, in shots that contain this optical illusion, whether it isn''t worth slightly over-rotating the whole thing to counter-act that. A touch darker overall would deepen the colour-tones here, which would be of use to the shot as a whole I think.', '2005-06-01 04:17:17.000000', NULL, 1),
(1425265, 183085, 35352, '<td valign="top">Very interesting. there are many sections of this photo that are captivating. I like the mist on the water and the haze of the trees on the other side.</td>', 'Very interesting. there are many sections of this photo that are captivating. I like the mist on the water and the haze of the trees on the other side.', '2005-06-01 04:40:26.000000', NULL, 1),
(1425271, 183303, 22748, '<td valign="top">Great lighting. I love the droplets.</td>', 'Great lighting. I love the droplets.', '2005-06-01 04:45:00.000000', NULL, 1),
(1425283, 181992, 22748, '<td valign="top">Really pretty. The simplicity of composition, the reflections, the silhouettes, really great. I predict top 10. But it''s hard to say how others will vote on this one, because I almost voted low, but after studying it, I''m voting much higher.<br/> <br/>The thing I''d change is I wish the mountains in the distance were in sharper focus. My first impulse was that the image was out of focus. The mountains looked out of focus and they caught my eye first and held it. Only once I intentionally focused on the swans and the close part of the lake did it become really beautiful. <br/> <br/>Actually, I might prefer a much closer composition, including only the swans, their wake, and the bottom half of the image or so, excluding the distant parts.</td>', 'Really pretty. The simplicity of composition, the reflections, the silhouettes, really great. I predict top 10. But it''s hard to say how others will vote on this one, because I almost voted low, but after studying it, I''m voting much higher. The thing I''d change is I wish the mountains in the distance were in sharper focus. My first impulse was that the image was out of focus. The mountains looked out of focus and they caught my eye first and held it. Only once I intentionally focused on the swans and the close part of the lake did it become really beautiful.  Actually, I might prefer a much closer composition, including only the swans, their wake, and the bottom half of the image or so, excluding the distant parts.', '2005-06-01 04:50:33.000000', NULL, 1),
(1425355, 182543, 24330, '<td valign="top">Looks just like my mother in law. LOL. <br/>Not sure composition is at its best, try a crop just below the horns, puts the eyes less central<br/>detail / colour great. love it</td>', 'Looks just like my mother in law. LOL. Not sure composition is at its best, try a crop just below the horns, puts the eyes less centraldetail / colour great. love it', '2005-06-01 06:20:17.000000', NULL, 1),
(1425356, 181992, 27482, '<td valign="top">Composition a little to centered for my taste but the colours and tones in this image are superb, good job!</td>', 'Composition a little to centered for my taste but the colours and tones in this image are superb, good job!', '2005-06-01 06:20:53.000000', NULL, 1),
(1425358, 183323, 27482, '<td valign="top">Framed a little bit too tightly for my taste, I don´t really appreciate the fact that you cut out both the front and the back of the tires and the top of the boy on the left but other than that I like this image, great tones and contrast and looks like it´s a very good moment you captured there.  Good job.</td>', 'Framed a little bit too tightly for my taste, I don´t really appreciate the fact that you cut out both the front and the back of the tires and the top of the boy on the left but other than that I like this image, great tones and contrast and looks like it´s a very good moment you captured there.  Good job.', '2005-06-01 06:25:15.000000', NULL, 1),
(1425361, 182987, 27482, '<td valign="top">Not bad but next time when you take an eye shot, try doing it outside on a sunny day, that will cause the iris to close down more and that way you get more colour and less black pupil.  For the shot itself, neither bad nor good IMO, gave it a 5.</td>', 'Not bad but next time when you take an eye shot, try doing it outside on a sunny day, that will cause the iris to close down more and that way you get more colour and less black pupil.  For the shot itself, neither bad nor good IMO, gave it a 5.', '2005-06-01 06:29:49.000000', NULL, 1),
(1425368, 182209, 6999, '<td valign="top">I find the light a bit harsh here - and this coast can look stunning in the first sun of the day. Good colouring, and well presented detail for an image with our size restrictions, and the sheer interetst of Amalfi generally give the shot some impact, but my immediate and abiding thought is that with the right light it could have had a real touch of magic.</td>', 'I find the light a bit harsh here - and this coast can look stunning in the first sun of the day. Good colouring, and well presented detail for an image with our size restrictions, and the sheer interetst of Amalfi generally give the shot some impact, but my immediate and abiding thought is that with the right light it could have had a real touch of magic.', '2005-06-01 06:36:44.000000', NULL, 1),
(1425370, 183021, 6999, '<td valign="top">... and missing part of a leg, it would seem. It''s always quite hard to get beyond the sheer scientific interest in macros like this, so there is some immediate impact from that alone; i half-like the composition - certainly the graphic nature of the shot the bokeh, the red and green appeals, but I''m unconvinved, I think, of your precise choice of framing in your crop.</td>', '... and missing part of a leg, it would seem. It''s always quite hard to get beyond the sheer scientific interest in macros like this, so there is some immediate impact from that alone; i half-like the composition - certainly the graphic nature of the shot the bokeh, the red and green appeals, but I''m unconvinved, I think, of your precise choice of framing in your crop.', '2005-06-01 06:41:30.000000', NULL, 1),
(1425374, 182995, 6999, '<td valign="top">Lovely tonality, composition - such near abstract graphic qualities in a photograph are, O know, deceptively simple to look at and hard to find in reality - you do well here. Strong sense of detail and texture, but the white areas of image left confuse things for me - half looking light over-exposed reflections of something, or perhaps a fungal thing, or paint, and that indecision drags at the mind, I find. But I like the sense of chaos, and more particularly I''m delighted to find someone who doesn''t just see beauty in the bland and straight-forward.</td>', 'Lovely tonality, composition - such near abstract graphic qualities in a photograph are, O know, deceptively simple to look at and hard to find in reality - you do well here. Strong sense of detail and texture, but the white areas of image left confuse things for me - half looking light over-exposed reflections of something, or perhaps a fungal thing, or paint, and that indecision drags at the mind, I find. But I like the sense of chaos, and more particularly I''m delighted to find someone who doesn''t just see beauty in the bland and straight-forward.', '2005-06-01 06:45:42.000000', NULL, 1),
(1425376, 183315, 6999, '<td valign="top">Whilst you are certainly at liberty to find beauty in a flower, I am also at liberty to find it simply pretty, and also to make that distinction quite strongly. That said, this is well photographed, and holds interest in its way.</td>', 'Whilst you are certainly at liberty to find beauty in a flower, I am also at liberty to find it simply pretty, and also to make that distinction quite strongly. That said, this is well photographed, and holds interest in its way.', '2005-06-01 06:47:36.000000', NULL, 1),
(1425378, 182918, 6999, '<td valign="top">A fine pet portrait, certainly; although I suspect some would find the close-cropping outside their limits of acceptibility :-( <br/> <br/>The execution is more or less impeccable - the even light, the focus, detail, la la la. I''m afraid it doesn''t excite, though - not for this viewer.</td>', 'A fine pet portrait, certainly; although I suspect some would find the close-cropping outside their limits of acceptibility :-(  The execution is more or less impeccable - the even light, the focus, detail, la la la. I''m afraid it doesn''t excite, though - not for this viewer.', '2005-06-01 06:50:00.000000', NULL, 1),
(1425380, 183324, 6999, '<td valign="top">The light is interesting, certainly, and effectively and cleverly done. Technically a fine photograph, but for me lacking any greater interest than the simply technical.</td>', 'The light is interesting, certainly, and effectively and cleverly done. Technically a fine photograph, but for me lacking any greater interest than the simply technical.', '2005-06-01 06:53:15.000000', NULL, 1),
(1425384, 183041, 6999, '<td valign="top">In this apparent glut of flower shots, this is a little better - there should, surely, be something beyind the simply pretty to qualify for ''beauty'', and this certainly makes statements about the progression, about the force, the puposefulness of the spring processes. These little earthquakes happen all around us, all the time, and it''s one of the points of photography to concentrate on such things. very fine work.</td>', 'In this apparent glut of flower shots, this is a little better - there should, surely, be something beyind the simply pretty to qualify for ''beauty'', and this certainly makes statements about the progression, about the force, the puposefulness of the spring processes. These little earthquakes happen all around us, all the time, and it''s one of the points of photography to concentrate on such things. very fine work.', '2005-06-01 06:55:26.000000', NULL, 1),
(1425387, 183270, 6999, '<td valign="top">I would have this sharper - would want to feel the grain in the particulate matter, fell the roughness of it all. You provoke interesting thoughts about the blance of beauty, about the desperate measures our world prompts in some people in it''s pusuit or denial, and I am of course happy to accept your decisions in your photograph.</td>', 'I would have this sharper - would want to feel the grain in the particulate matter, fell the roughness of it all. You provoke interesting thoughts about the blance of beauty, about the desperate measures our world prompts in some people in it''s pusuit or denial, and I am of course happy to accept your decisions in your photograph.', '2005-06-01 06:58:17.000000', NULL, 1),
(1425389, 183212, 6999, '<td valign="top">Assured, effective, quite interesting graphically, slightly different. It''s certainly a clever shot - but beautiful? I''m uncertain of such isolation and <i>style</i> imposed on things ...</td>', 'Assured, effective, quite interesting graphically, slightly different. It''s certainly a clever shot - but beautiful? I''m uncertain of such isolation and style imposed on things ...', '2005-06-01 07:01:33.000000', NULL, 1),
(1425390, 182525, 6999, '<td valign="top">The order in which photographs appear is random, so it''s pure misfortune that I''m so very very very bored of flower shots now.</td>', 'The order in which photographs appear is random, so it''s pure misfortune that I''m so very very very bored of flower shots now.', '2005-06-01 07:02:28.000000', NULL, 1),
(1425391, 183338, 6999, '<td valign="top">Hurrah! Hurrah! You get a ten, if only because it isn''t a photograph of a flower ;-)</td>', 'Hurrah! Hurrah! You get a ten, if only because it isn''t a photograph of a flower ;-)', '2005-06-01 07:03:48.000000', NULL, 1),
(1425394, 183189, 6999, '<td valign="top">For me this entire shot is over-exposed - there is so little that is finctioning ona  brightness level below ''quite intense'' - and it''s so difficult to find texture and interesting depth of tonality in this light.  To be fair, you''ve shot in a quite harsh light, and it''s not easy to find a graceful sense of texture and shade in that. The solution is probably simply to shoot at a different time of day :-(</td>', 'For me this entire shot is over-exposed - there is so little that is finctioning ona  brightness level below ''quite intense'' - and it''s so difficult to find texture and interesting depth of tonality in this light.  To be fair, you''ve shot in a quite harsh light, and it''s not easy to find a graceful sense of texture and shade in that. The solution is probably simply to shoot at a different time of day :-(', '2005-06-01 07:06:44.000000', NULL, 1),
(1425461, 182606, 9780, '<td valign="top">Dark and mistarius 7</td>', 'Dark and mistarius 7', '2005-06-01 08:06:03.000000', NULL, 1),
(1425467, 182292, 9780, '<td valign="top">nice negative space. lovly colores. 8<br/></td>', 'nice negative space. lovly colores. 8', '2005-06-01 08:08:42.000000', NULL, 1),
(1425469, 183340, 9780, '<td valign="top">Is this real???</td>', 'Is this real???', '2005-06-01 08:09:21.000000', NULL, 1),
(1425476, 183176, 9780, '<td valign="top">:) nice job!</td>', ':) nice job!', '2005-06-01 08:18:09.000000', NULL, 1),
(1425514, 182772, 5822, '<td valign="top">Despite the uninteresting and blown out sky, I like this image very much. The tones in the bottom half are superb and painterly. Had you shifted up the horizon to include less of the sky it may have gotten an even higher mark from me. 8</td>', 'Despite the uninteresting and blown out sky, I like this image very much. The tones in the bottom half are superb and painterly. Had you shifted up the horizon to include less of the sky it may have gotten an even higher mark from me. 8', '2005-06-01 08:54:42.000000', NULL, 1),
(1425529, 183041, 24925, '<td valign="top">Nice capture with good texture, but I think the composition could have used some more experimentation...</td>', 'Nice capture with good texture, but I think the composition could have used some more experimentation...', '2005-06-01 09:01:31.000000', NULL, 1),
(1425535, 183115, 24925, '<td valign="top">sure, why not?  this works...I bet it''s much more stunning at full size...</td>', 'sure, why not?  this works...I bet it''s much more stunning at full size...', '2005-06-01 09:02:37.000000', NULL, 1),
(1425580, 182280, 25024, '<td valign="top">Nice pose, nice lighting - a real beauty! My only constructive criticism is the hands being so much darker than the rest of this lovely image dont quite look as though they belong to her, but its still a cracking photo, good luck</td>', 'Nice pose, nice lighting - a real beauty! My only constructive criticism is the hands being so much darker than the rest of this lovely image dont quite look as though they belong to her, but its still a cracking photo, good luck', '2005-06-01 09:19:16.000000', NULL, 1),
(1425587, 182716, 25024, '<td valign="top">Excellent capture this and what a beauty! Great pose and very effective extremes of black and white framing her.</td>', 'Excellent capture this and what a beauty! Great pose and very effective extremes of black and white framing her.', '2005-06-01 09:22:34.000000', NULL, 1),
