(1430759, 183317, 30625, '<td valign="top">Challenge: 7 As for animals I love dangerous cat species. It just doesnt tell me wow or thats beautiful.<br/>Compostion: 6 I wish there was more than just there heads. Cats have some great curves  created by there bodies.<br/>Technical: 7 sharp, colors look as though they could have used a little more hue. <br/>Overall: 7</td>', 'Challenge: 7 As for animals I love dangerous cat species. It just doesnt tell me wow or thats beautiful.Compostion: 6 I wish there was more than just there heads. Cats have some great curves  created by there bodies.Technical: 7 sharp, colors look as though they could have used a little more hue. Overall: 7', '2005-06-03 03:09:19.000000', NULL, 1),
(1430775, 183085, 6999, '<td valign="top">Now this, to my eye, really <i>is</i> beautiful - because, I would say, it''s about more than a simply pleasing scene or moment, and moves into the area of complication, of things suggested and unsaid, and it is that delightful ability of the art that nakes photography such a powerful thing. You capture a mood fantastically.</td>', 'Now this, to my eye, really is beautiful - because, I would say, it''s about more than a simply pleasing scene or moment, and moves into the area of complication, of things suggested and unsaid, and it is that delightful ability of the art that nakes photography such a powerful thing. You capture a mood fantastically.', '2005-06-03 03:38:02.000000', NULL, 1),
(1430780, 183066, 6999, '<td valign="top">Certainly a wonderful location. Fpr one thing, however, you have chosen a poor light to make an attractive shot - this very overhead sun leads only to a very high contrast between the grass and the trees - if you werre to darken this tto the level you need to to get some life into the colour of the grass, the trees would become nothing more than black lumps. The composition is well seen though - andd the use of that path to lead the eye is clever. Not wholly sure about your placemtn of that rock, though - it''s cutting into the edge of frame makes it seem an acciddental inclusion, rather than a compositional decision.</td>', 'Certainly a wonderful location. Fpr one thing, however, you have chosen a poor light to make an attractive shot - this very overhead sun leads only to a very high contrast between the grass and the trees - if you werre to darken this tto the level you need to to get some life into the colour of the grass, the trees would become nothing more than black lumps. The composition is well seen though - andd the use of that path to lead the eye is clever. Not wholly sure about your placemtn of that rock, though - it''s cutting into the edge of frame makes it seem an acciddental inclusion, rather than a compositional decision.', '2005-06-03 03:42:45.000000', NULL, 1),
(1430784, 182952, 6999, '<td valign="top">Great shot. I would surely have wanted to show this in black and white: the image would be more about the expressions and textures, and I think the colour tones, whilst perfectly well caught for sure, to me seem to have nothing to do with the power of the shot. Also, people''s reaction to black and white is more likely to give an image a quality of seriousness that this image surely deserves. Wonderful work.</td>', 'Great shot. I would surely have wanted to show this in black and white: the image would be more about the expressions and textures, and I think the colour tones, whilst perfectly well caught for sure, to me seem to have nothing to do with the power of the shot. Also, people''s reaction to black and white is more likely to give an image a quality of seriousness that this image surely deserves. Wonderful work.', '2005-06-03 03:46:19.000000', NULL, 1),
(1430785, 181170, 38619, '<td valign="top">magnificent!</td>', 'magnificent!', '2005-06-03 03:48:41.000000', NULL, 1),
(1430786, 182906, 38619, '<td valign="top">paradise</td>', 'paradise', '2005-06-03 03:49:00.000000', NULL, 1),
(1430788, 183161, 38619, '<td valign="top">peacefullllllllll</td>', 'peacefullllllllll', '2005-06-03 03:50:20.000000', NULL, 1),
(1430790, 182998, 6999, '<td valign="top">Amusing shot. Your colour balance is strange, point of view is very ordinary, focus seems a touch soft - at least there is certainly not the level of fine detail one would really want here - and the exposure seems very flat, lacking contrast. It''s only the subject that makes this at all interesting to me - I''m not sure that''s enough.</td>', 'Amusing shot. Your colour balance is strange, point of view is very ordinary, focus seems a touch soft - at least there is certainly not the level of fine detail one would really want here - and the exposure seems very flat, lacking contrast. It''s only the subject that makes this at all interesting to me - I''m not sure that''s enough.', '2005-06-03 03:52:20.000000', NULL, 1),
(1430796, 183072, 30532, '<td valign="top">This shot is very pretty!  I''ve spent many hours trying to capture such a picture.</td>', 'This shot is very pretty!  I''ve spent many hours trying to capture such a picture.', '2005-06-03 04:02:12.000000', NULL, 1),
(1430808, 183334, 32602, '<td valign="top">Love the light coming through the petals, the luminescent white around the stamens. Nice colour choice.</td>', 'Love the light coming through the petals, the luminescent white around the stamens. Nice colour choice.', '2005-06-03 04:19:05.000000', NULL, 1),
(1430839, 183339, 6999, '<td valign="top">I like the sense of tonality in the shade areas of this image, but I feel that the highlight areas are too far blown out for the viewer''s comfort: it seems to have been exposed directly for the shade, and to hell with the highlights - I think you would get more detail and an image easier on the eye by starting from a more compromise exposure, and working it up from there. Of course, if this is what you envisaged, then I just don''t get it, huh?</td>', 'I like the sense of tonality in the shade areas of this image, but I feel that the highlight areas are too far blown out for the viewer''s comfort: it seems to have been exposed directly for the shade, and to hell with the highlights - I think you would get more detail and an image easier on the eye by starting from a more compromise exposure, and working it up from there. Of course, if this is what you envisaged, then I just don''t get it, huh?', '2005-06-03 05:15:22.000000', NULL, 1),
(1430847, 183214, 6999, '<td valign="top">I kind of like what seems to be the root of this image, but I don''t much care at all for whatever it is that your processing has done to it - were it not for the depth of field, I would say it looks just like a 150% crop from a Fuji digital compact. Most odd, but too much about the weird process thing than about photography - in fact, I think you''ve actually masked the photography with this processing.</td>', 'I kind of like what seems to be the root of this image, but I don''t much care at all for whatever it is that your processing has done to it - were it not for the depth of field, I would say it looks just like a 150% crop from a Fuji digital compact. Most odd, but too much about the weird process thing than about photography - in fact, I think you''ve actually masked the photography with this processing.', '2005-06-03 05:19:14.000000', NULL, 1),
(1430850, 181290, 6999, '<td valign="top">Obviously competent stuff - I fear I find such games with composition rather dull, however.</td>', 'Obviously competent stuff - I fear I find such games with composition rather dull, however.', '2005-06-03 05:20:32.000000', NULL, 1),
(1430893, 181386, 6999, '<td valign="top">I like your sense of composition - there''s certainly some movement to this presentation. Sky is good, I wonder if perhaps a little more ping from the greens might have given it some more attention-grabbing power.</td>', 'I like your sense of composition - there''s certainly some movement to this presentation. Sky is good, I wonder if perhaps a little more ping from the greens might have given it some more attention-grabbing power.', '2005-06-03 06:39:29.000000', NULL, 1),
