(1432417, 183339, 30791, '<td valign="top">i used to live in crabtree northcarolina a few years ago</td>', 'i used to live in crabtree northcarolina a few years ago', '2005-06-04 01:02:19.000000', NULL, 1),
(1432418, 182751, 30791, '<td valign="top">oh yeah, thats amazing 9</td>', 'oh yeah, thats amazing 9', '2005-06-04 01:02:59.000000', NULL, 1),
(1432421, 183214, 30791, '<td valign="top">i normally dont like floral pictures, but this aone appeals to me, great job<br/>8</td>', 'i normally dont like floral pictures, but this aone appeals to me, great job8', '2005-06-04 01:04:24.000000', NULL, 1),
(1432423, 182261, 30791, '<td valign="top">hahah cool</td>', 'hahah cool', '2005-06-04 01:04:48.000000', NULL, 1),
(1432425, 183158, 38648, '<td valign="top">Very cool</td>', 'Very cool', '2005-06-04 01:05:33.000000', NULL, 1),
(1432436, 182986, 8891, '<td valign="top">Like the hi key sepia tone and the beautiful subject with all the flowing fabric about her. I am distracted by the piles of packages(?) on both sides and the women on the right. I think they could have been cropped without losing too much of your subject.</td>', 'Like the hi key sepia tone and the beautiful subject with all the flowing fabric about her. I am distracted by the piles of packages(?) on both sides and the women on the right. I think they could have been cropped without losing too much of your subject.', '2005-06-04 01:30:50.000000', NULL, 1),
(1432441, 183274, 8891, '<td valign="top">I like the rays at the bottom and the nice silhouette of the tree. The tree gets a little lost at its top and left side in the dark of the sky....I am not a dodging burning expert at al...trust me...but I think a bit of judicous dodging about the tree in the aforementioned areas might have helped the tree to stand out more.  Nice work none-the less.</td>', 'I like the rays at the bottom and the nice silhouette of the tree. The tree gets a little lost at its top and left side in the dark of the sky....I am not a dodging burning expert at al...trust me...but I think a bit of judicous dodging about the tree in the aforementioned areas might have helped the tree to stand out more.  Nice work none-the less.', '2005-06-04 01:34:25.000000', NULL, 1),
(1432445, 183080, 8891, '<td valign="top">Very nice image in a very classic style. Like the softness of the meadow flowers and the costume on your model. Even in profile it is evident that the subject is lovely but seeing more of her visage might work better for this, IMO, as well as having the headpiece either smaller or back a bit off of her face. The crop is a bit too tight for my tastes and I would have liked to have seen more of the field about her.</td>', 'Very nice image in a very classic style. Like the softness of the meadow flowers and the costume on your model. Even in profile it is evident that the subject is lovely but seeing more of her visage might work better for this, IMO, as well as having the headpiece either smaller or back a bit off of her face. The crop is a bit too tight for my tastes and I would have liked to have seen more of the field about her.', '2005-06-04 01:38:54.000000', NULL, 1),
(1432446, 183114, 8891, '<td valign="top">Shooting birds is not my forté and capturing them has daunted me. I have never gotten one half as good as this. I like the detail of the neck and the crown.  THe detail is a bit lost under the beak and I think the subject to high up in the frame. Love that brilliant blue eye.</td>', 'Shooting birds is not my forté and capturing them has daunted me. I have never gotten one half as good as this. I like the detail of the neck and the crown.  THe detail is a bit lost under the beak and I think the subject to high up in the frame. Love that brilliant blue eye.', '2005-06-04 01:41:56.000000', NULL, 1),
(1432449, 183334, 8891, '<td valign="top">Like th detail and compositon on this a lot. Really like the tones you chose cause these hearts can come real bright in hot light. Excellent DOF.</td>', 'Like th detail and compositon on this a lot. Really like the tones you chose cause these hearts can come real bright in hot light. Excellent DOF.', '2005-06-04 01:44:34.000000', NULL, 1),
(1432453, 182918, 8891, '<td valign="top">Super portrait of this Spaniel. I am enjoying the detail of this canine very mucy as well as the beautiful sad expression. THe chocice of background was good as there colors in it that compliment the coloring of the detail the dog. I''m sure...well let''s say I am positive you might have gotten something about the cropping off of the top of the head but that has not bothered my viewing of this image at all. Wow! Great.. excellent image.</td>', 'Super portrait of this Spaniel. I am enjoying the detail of this canine very mucy as well as the beautiful sad expression. THe chocice of background was good as there colors in it that compliment the coloring of the detail the dog. I''m sure...well let''s say I am positive you might have gotten something about the cropping off of the top of the head but that has not bothered my viewing of this image at all. Wow! Great.. excellent image.', '2005-06-04 01:48:45.000000', NULL, 1),
(1432459, 183270, 8891, '<td valign="top">This is just a very striking image....beautiful? hmm....well in ways yes...more like anti-beautiful....the lack of apparent beauty perhaps is the message but one can find beauty in most everything if you open your mind to it. But it all does not matter in the long run. There is some much to see in this and it tells a story which not be considered beautiful either...but it says something. I hope to figure out what. Great work....hope you''re not getting too bashed for not meeting the challenge.</td>', 'This is just a very striking image....beautiful? hmm....well in ways yes...more like anti-beautiful....the lack of apparent beauty perhaps is the message but one can find beauty in most everything if you open your mind to it. But it all does not matter in the long run. There is some much to see in this and it tells a story which not be considered beautiful either...but it says something. I hope to figure out what. Great work....hope you''re not getting too bashed for not meeting the challenge.', '2005-06-04 01:57:38.000000', NULL, 1),
(1432462, 183335, 20168, '<td valign="top">Bird takes the shot to another level, especially that little gull strut going on.  Great entry. 10</td>', 'Bird takes the shot to another level, especially that little gull strut going on.  Great entry. 10', '2005-06-04 02:01:44.000000', NULL, 1),
(1432465, 182209, 37334, '<td valign="top">I''ve always wanted to go here....So much to look at in your image! Well captured;) 9</td>', 'I''ve always wanted to go here....So much to look at in your image! Well captured;) 9', '2005-06-04 02:04:21.000000', NULL, 1),
(1432476, 181634, 37334, '<td valign="top">I''m sure I left a comment on this before! I love this image...it works on so many levels and conveys so many emotions...It is brave and honest, and beautiful...It has really moved me. Thank you! 10<br/></td>', 'I''m sure I left a comment on this before! I love this image...it works on so many levels and conveys so many emotions...It is brave and honest, and beautiful...It has really moved me. Thank you! 10', '2005-06-04 02:16:57.000000', NULL, 1),
(1432477, 182211, 37334, '<td valign="top">I really like this - the image I mean. I love the way it seems to be hovering in mid air.8</td>', 'I really like this - the image I mean. I love the way it seems to be hovering in mid air.8', '2005-06-04 02:18:27.000000', NULL, 1),
(1432487, 183019, 21991, '<td valign="top">this is gorgeous, the natural green-yellow gradient looks like a painting</td>', 'this is gorgeous, the natural green-yellow gradient looks like a painting', '2005-06-04 02:39:01.000000', NULL, 1),
(1432491, 182772, 25355, '<td valign="top">This looks like a painting. Lovely rural scene.</td>', 'This looks like a painting. Lovely rural scene.', '2005-06-04 02:41:06.000000', NULL, 1),
(1432495, 182751, 30861, '<td valign="top">This is quite spectacular and does bring me back for more looks; but the more I look, the more I wish there was a trace of detail in the deep shade. Probably not possible with the exposure you made, I guess. Whatever, a strong entry.</td>', 'This is quite spectacular and does bring me back for more looks; but the more I look, the more I wish there was a trace of detail in the deep shade. Probably not possible with the exposure you made, I guess. Whatever, a strong entry.', '2005-06-04 02:46:42.000000', NULL, 1),
(1432497, 182648, 16790, '<td valign="top">Mmm.. beautiful indeed.  Usually shadows bother me, but in this case I like them - they add some nice drama to the simple background.  Lighting is great - again, I like the shadows and highlights.  Expression is fantastic, pose is perfect, and the composition is very effective - 10!</td>', 'Mmm.. beautiful indeed.  Usually shadows bother me, but in this case I like them - they add some nice drama to the simple background.  Lighting is great - again, I like the shadows and highlights.  Expression is fantastic, pose is perfect, and the composition is very effective - 10!', '2005-06-04 02:49:21.000000', NULL, 1),
(1432499, 181725, 30861, '<td valign="top">Sweetly done. Compositionally, the eye of the vortex seems too centered to me. The entire area to the right lacks any real textural OR composional interst. I have tried cropping it into a square and this seems to work better, though it''s not ideal. Composion aside, the lighting and the color are exceptionally nice.</td>', 'Sweetly done. Compositionally, the eye of the vortex seems too centered to me. The entire area to the right lacks any real textural OR composional interst. I have tried cropping it into a square and this seems to work better, though it''s not ideal. Composion aside, the lighting and the color are exceptionally nice.', '2005-06-04 02:49:55.000000', NULL, 1),
(1432500, 182959, 16790, '<td valign="top">This is absolutely beautiful - not just because the subject is lovely, but because the colours, sharpness, composition, etc. is all exactly what it needs to be to make this a stunning photograph.  I love the slight feel of undersaturation, with the little bits of pink accenting here and there.  This is just marvelous - 10.</td>', 'This is absolutely beautiful - not just because the subject is lovely, but because the colours, sharpness, composition, etc. is all exactly what it needs to be to make this a stunning photograph.  I love the slight feel of undersaturation, with the little bits of pink accenting here and there.  This is just marvelous - 10.', '2005-06-04 02:51:53.000000', NULL, 1),
(1432502, 182726, 16790, '<td valign="top">I''m a sucker for a spider web, and the beaded water drops are perfectly captured here.  Lovely work - sharpness is excellent, composition works well; I''d like if the dark bits were a tad closer to black-black, but - regardless - this is awesome work.</td>', 'I''m a sucker for a spider web, and the beaded water drops are perfectly captured here.  Lovely work - sharpness is excellent, composition works well; I''d like if the dark bits were a tad closer to black-black, but - regardless - this is awesome work.', '2005-06-04 02:52:51.000000', NULL, 1),
(1432503, 183333, 30861, '<td valign="top">This certainly is the strangest image in the challenge. You get bravery points just for including some not-especially-beautiful feet in a beauty challenge :-) I''m torn on this one, because the image is very appealing to me in an offbeat way, but it hardly seems to address the challenge. On the other hand, who am I to judge what''s beautiful? The picture brings me back, and back again, so I''m gonna bump it up, and wish you the best :-)<br/> <br/>This from the man that entered a raindrop as a self-portrait, remember...</td>', 'This certainly is the strangest image in the challenge. You get bravery points just for including some not-especially-beautiful feet in a beauty challenge :-) I''m torn on this one, because the image is very appealing to me in an offbeat way, but it hardly seems to address the challenge. On the other hand, who am I to judge what''s beautiful? The picture brings me back, and back again, so I''m gonna bump it up, and wish you the best :-) This from the man that entered a raindrop as a self-portrait, remember...', '2005-06-04 02:53:07.000000', NULL, 1),
(1432505, 183307, 30861, '<td valign="top">This is quite lovely. I wish the ,oon weren''t quite so centered, and I don''t think the bright light on the right horizon is helping at all, so I''d have thought about panning left a little to get the composition a tad less static. regardless, nice and imaginative work and a strong entry.</td>', 'This is quite lovely. I wish the ,oon weren''t quite so centered, and I don''t think the bright light on the right horizon is helping at all, so I''d have thought about panning left a little to get the composition a tad less static. regardless, nice and imaginative work and a strong entry.', '2005-06-04 02:55:02.000000', NULL, 1),
(1432506, 182952, 16790, '<td valign="top">I love this one!  The clarity is stunning, composition is brilliant, and there is some really lovely bokeh going on too.  And somehow the "new" element of the mother and the "old fashioned" element of her beautiful child really combine to make this not only gorgeous but interesting and unique.  Excellent work!</td>', 'I love this one!  The clarity is stunning, composition is brilliant, and there is some really lovely bokeh going on too.  And somehow the "new" element of the mother and the "old fashioned" element of her beautiful child really combine to make this not only gorgeous but interesting and unique.  Excellent work!', '2005-06-04 02:55:32.000000', NULL, 1),
(1432508, 182209, 30861, '<td valign="top">Deceptively simple image that appeals to me immensely. I wish it were crisper. It''s very nicely framed and, personally, I think it''s quite strong. But I''ve always liked "busy" pictures with no obvious subject, and they rarely seem to do well in DPC, so I wish you the best of luck with this one. Strong score from me.</td>', 'Deceptively simple image that appeals to me immensely. I wish it were crisper. It''s very nicely framed and, personally, I think it''s quite strong. But I''ve always liked "busy" pictures with no obvious subject, and they rarely seem to do well in DPC, so I wish you the best of luck with this one. Strong score from me.', '2005-06-04 02:56:58.000000', NULL, 1),
(1432511, 183019, 16790, '<td valign="top">The simplicity of this, and the smooth colour transitions really give this photograph a lot of appeal.  It has almost an abstract quality in that I see the colours and immediately feel a sense of tranquility before I absorb the contents of the foreground and background; this is definitely a very beautiful work of art.  Nice job!</td>', 'The simplicity of this, and the smooth colour transitions really give this photograph a lot of appeal.  It has almost an abstract quality in that I see the colours and immediately feel a sense of tranquility before I absorb the contents of the foreground and background; this is definitely a very beautiful work of art.  Nice job!', '2005-06-04 02:58:18.000000', NULL, 1),
(1432512, 183031, 30861, '<td valign="top">Conceptually this is exceptionally nice, but there''s a harsh garishness to it that isn''t working that well for me. Also, the yellowish central portion of the image is out of critical focus, and yet that''s the area our eyes are migrating to, so more DOF or focusing in a bit would have helped a lot here. The reddisha rea upper left is a real eyetrap also. This being advanced editing, it would have been easy to desaturate that area so it faded back a bit, and this would have been a plus. Still, a nice, strong image and a good score from me.</td>', 'Conceptually this is exceptionally nice, but there''s a harsh garishness to it that isn''t working that well for me. Also, the yellowish central portion of the image is out of critical focus, and yet that''s the area our eyes are migrating to, so more DOF or focusing in a bit would have helped a lot here. The reddisha rea upper left is a real eyetrap also. This being advanced editing, it would have been easy to desaturate that area so it faded back a bit, and this would have been a plus. Still, a nice, strong image and a good score from me.', '2005-06-04 02:59:53.000000', NULL, 1),
(1432514, 182357, 29486, '<td valign="top">Very nice capture of a really quick bird</td>', 'Very nice capture of a really quick bird', '2005-06-04 03:00:44.000000', NULL, 1),
(1432516, 182692, 16790, '<td valign="top">This is a lovely portrait - it imparts a real feeling of character, and the background colour works brilliantly to make the photograph feel complete.  I like the sense of motion with her hair; it lends a free, upbeat feel to the picture that compliments her smile and shiny eyes.  My only complaint is that I see a few distracting artifacts (compression?), particularly in the hair/background.  Regardless, a lovely, solid photograph - 9.</td>', 'This is a lovely portrait - it imparts a real feeling of character, and the background colour works brilliantly to make the photograph feel complete.  I like the sense of motion with her hair; it lends a free, upbeat feel to the picture that compliments her smile and shiny eyes.  My only complaint is that I see a few distracting artifacts (compression?), particularly in the hair/background.  Regardless, a lovely, solid photograph - 9.', '2005-06-04 03:01:27.000000', NULL, 1),
(1432517, 182693, 30861, '<td valign="top">This is quite beautiful and well-seen. I have two nits, basically:<br/> <br/>1. There''s visible evidence of oversharpening all along the horizon on the left. There are zeveral ways to fix thisin PS, including just using less sharpening; I don''t think the image needs to be this sharp, certainly not in the sky/tree area. You could have made a selection of the foreground dune only and just sharpened that area very profitably.<br/> <br/>2. The placement of the tree is distinctly arbitrary, it leaves an area to the right that''s quite uncomfortable to my eye. I have tried cropping out half of that area, bringing the right edge closer to the tree, and IMO this improved the composition dramatically.<br/> <br/>Regardless, it''s a strong entry and I hope it does well.</td>', 'This is quite beautiful and well-seen. I have two nits, basically: 1. There''s visible evidence of oversharpening all along the horizon on the left. There are zeveral ways to fix thisin PS, including just using less sharpening; I don''t think the image needs to be this sharp, certainly not in the sky/tree area. You could have made a selection of the foreground dune only and just sharpened that area very profitably. 2. The placement of the tree is distinctly arbitrary, it leaves an area to the right that''s quite uncomfortable to my eye. I have tried cropping out half of that area, bringing the right edge closer to the tree, and IMO this improved the composition dramatically. Regardless, it''s a strong entry and I hope it does well.', '2005-06-04 03:05:18.000000', NULL, 1),
(1432518, 182918, 29486, '<td valign="top">Perfect shot except for the contrast/color.  If you could have bumped them up making the picture pop then it would be super.</td>', 'Perfect shot except for the contrast/color.  If you could have bumped them up making the picture pop then it would be super.', '2005-06-04 03:05:30.000000', NULL, 1),
(1432519, 182111, 16790, '<td valign="top">First let me say that you''ve probably already heard about the noise, so I''m not going to talk about it much.  It doesn''t really bother me; there is perhaps a tad too much, but it''s not enough to take much at all away from this photograph for me.  I think you''ve done a marvelous job of catching some of this beautiful animal''s spirit on [not film - um, digital media? :)] and I love the way the light, shadows, and lovely, smooth background look.  The bright sky fits - the shadows and highlights are right on to my eye.  I also like the crop/composition - lovely photograph!  Lots of personality. 8.</td>', 'First let me say that you''ve probably already heard about the noise, so I''m not going to talk about it much.  It doesn''t really bother me; there is perhaps a tad too much, but it''s not enough to take much at all away from this photograph for me.  I think you''ve done a marvelous job of catching some of this beautiful animal''s spirit on [not film - um, digital media? :)] and I love the way the light, shadows, and lovely, smooth background look.  The bright sky fits - the shadows and highlights are right on to my eye.  I also like the crop/composition - lovely photograph!  Lots of personality. 8.', '2005-06-04 03:05:31.000000', NULL, 1),
(1432521, 183049, 16790, '<td valign="top">Awwwwwwwwww!  First off, I love the colours; secondly, I''m a sucker for a little kitty in any sort of little container.  In this case, the pretty bowl works well, and the kitty is absolutely adorable.  Composition is nice; colours all look good, and the sharpness is decent.  I see some mild noise or perhaps compression artifacts in the red, but red always seems to show that too much, so it doesn''t take away IMO.  Adorable!  Nice shot.</td>', 'Awwwwwwwwww!  First off, I love the colours; secondly, I''m a sucker for a little kitty in any sort of little container.  In this case, the pretty bowl works well, and the kitty is absolutely adorable.  Composition is nice; colours all look good, and the sharpness is decent.  I see some mild noise or perhaps compression artifacts in the red, but red always seems to show that too much, so it doesn''t take away IMO.  Adorable!  Nice shot.', '2005-06-04 03:07:07.000000', NULL, 1),
(1432522, 183205, 29486, '<td valign="top">Superb except for the feet.  They are nicely out of focus but they still draw so much attention.</td>', 'Superb except for the feet.  They are nicely out of focus but they still draw so much attention.', '2005-06-04 03:07:49.000000', NULL, 1),
(1432523, 181992, 30861, '<td valign="top">The horizon running downhill to the right and the strange lack of luminosity in what should, by rights, be a hauntingly luminous scene detract from this very well seen and basically very beautiful image. 6 from me.</td>', 'The horizon running downhill to the right and the strange lack of luminosity in what should, by rights, be a hauntingly luminous scene detract from this very well seen and basically very beautiful image. 6 from me.', '2005-06-04 03:07:57.000000', NULL, 1),
(1432524, 181953, 16046, '<td valign="top">Those are some big eyes, sharp, bumping up</td>', 'Those are some big eyes, sharp, bumping up', '2005-06-04 03:08:03.000000', NULL, 1),
(1432527, 182726, 16046, '<td valign="top">Nice pearls, well done, bumping up</td>', 'Nice pearls, well done, bumping up', '2005-06-04 03:09:25.000000', NULL, 1),
(1432531, 183213, 16046, '<td valign="top">Well done, nice image, bumping up</td>', 'Well done, nice image, bumping up', '2005-06-04 03:10:07.000000', NULL, 1),
(1432532, 183301, 30861, '<td valign="top">Almost completely without anythign to focus on, almost totally subject-less, this image becomes all about the muted sense of light, with even the colors downplayed (the temptation to shif them up in saturation must have been hard to resist). I like it quite a lot, but I suspect it is not faring well at the hands of the voters. From me, a 7.</td>', 'Almost completely without anythign to focus on, almost totally subject-less, this image becomes all about the muted sense of light, with even the colors downplayed (the temptation to shif them up in saturation must have been hard to resist). I like it quite a lot, but I suspect it is not faring well at the hands of the voters. From me, a 7.', '2005-06-04 03:10:14.000000', NULL, 1),
(1432534, 182111, 16046, '<td valign="top">looks grainey, but nice image, bumping up</td>', 'looks grainey, but nice image, bumping up', '2005-06-04 03:10:52.000000', NULL, 1),
(1432537, 182843, 16046, '<td valign="top">great wall paper, best of the peacocks, bumping up</td>', 'great wall paper, best of the peacocks, bumping up', '2005-06-04 03:11:28.000000', NULL, 1),
