(1435589, 183333, 17507, '<td valign="top"><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by sfalice:</b></div><hr/><i> Damon!  While I (er) stand by my remarks made during the competition, I was delighted to see there were several schools of thought on those toes of yours...  <br/> <br/>Hope you gave that gorgeous cat a good belly rub after you took his picture.<br/> <br/>Alice </i></td></tr></table> <br/> <br/>Hahah. Yes, my toes were not very popular. When I saw your comment, I giggled a bit to myself over the effects that anonymity during voting can have. But I like this picture, even if it finished in the 10th percentile!!!!!<br/> <br/>The kitty is well loved on a frequent basis, so don''t worry about that :) Thanks for commenting!</td>', 'Originally posted by sfalice: Damon!  While I (er) stand by my remarks made during the competition, I was delighted to see there were several schools of thought on those toes of yours...   Hope you gave that gorgeous cat a good belly rub after you took his picture. Alice   Hahah. Yes, my toes were not very popular. When I saw your comment, I giggled a bit to myself over the effects that anonymity during voting can have. But I like this picture, even if it finished in the 10th percentile!!!!! The kitty is well loved on a frequent basis, so don''t worry about that :) Thanks for commenting!', '2005-06-06 02:05:31.000000', NULL, 0),
(1435598, 183320, 9581, '<td valign="top">Well now I have to critique myself... John setzler had a thread about this about a month ago.. <br/> <br/>The white ring edging around my baby''s face is not helping the eye any at all. This is a little blurry as well as noisy. There is a shadow as well and perhaps this is because my aperature was set on f2.8...Perhaps if I had openeded it up to about f8 more light could of come through the camera and make this even more sharp. The sun was setting so I used a flash, and one of the worse things about my camera is if I use a filter with my ring adaptor this will cause a circle somewhere on my subject specially if it was a macro... <br/>I got out today and tried some more shots with the similar intensions. They came out far more better then this one did and just a bit too late... So I think I am starting to grasp the skills some....If I was voting though I would of gave this picture a 10 anyways... I love the smile.. hehehe I would though huh.. hes my joy!<br/></td>', 'Well now I have to critique myself... John setzler had a thread about this about a month ago..  The white ring edging around my baby''s face is not helping the eye any at all. This is a little blurry as well as noisy. There is a shadow as well and perhaps this is because my aperature was set on f2.8...Perhaps if I had openeded it up to about f8 more light could of come through the camera and make this even more sharp. The sun was setting so I used a flash, and one of the worse things about my camera is if I use a filter with my ring adaptor this will cause a circle somewhere on my subject specially if it was a macro... I got out today and tried some more shots with the similar intensions. They came out far more better then this one did and just a bit too late... So I think I am starting to grasp the skills some....If I was voting though I would of gave this picture a 10 anyways... I love the smile.. hehehe I would though huh.. hes my joy!', '2005-06-06 02:08:32.000000', NULL, 0),
