(1444717, 182965, 37149, '<td valign="top">thanks for the critique! This photo is full frame with what I shot... I realize now I should have kept the wing and abdomen in. I didn''t notice it because I was so focused on getting a good shot of the head of the butterfly.<br/> <br/>As for the lighting... this was in a butterfly garden, no choice in lighting and I did not use a flash or anything of that anture. All natural lighting in basically a greenhouse.<br/> <br/>As for the commenter who said it was oversharpened.... I only sharpened the eye and "tongue" of the butterfly to give it a bit more pop. Everything else is unaltered.<br/> <br/>I did a bit of saturation to make the colors pop a bit more but other than that, i did very little to this photograph, thought it was great as is for the most part.<br/> <br/>It''s hard to shoot butterflies and this trip I got very few useable shots. There were a LOT of people milling around and disturbing the butterflies which I found ANNOYING. I''ll have to take another trip to Magic Wings soon and try again.</td>', 'thanks for the critique! This photo is full frame with what I shot... I realize now I should have kept the wing and abdomen in. I didn''t notice it because I was so focused on getting a good shot of the head of the butterfly. As for the lighting... this was in a butterfly garden, no choice in lighting and I did not use a flash or anything of that anture. All natural lighting in basically a greenhouse. As for the commenter who said it was oversharpened.... I only sharpened the eye and "tongue" of the butterfly to give it a bit more pop. Everything else is unaltered. I did a bit of saturation to make the colors pop a bit more but other than that, i did very little to this photograph, thought it was great as is for the most part. It''s hard to shoot butterflies and this trip I got very few useable shots. There were a LOT of people milling around and disturbing the butterflies which I found ANNOYING. I''ll have to take another trip to Magic Wings soon and try again.', '2005-06-09 22:14:18.000000', NULL, 0),
